
X: 0
T: Kauntze's Collection of the most favorite Dances, Reels, Waltzes, &c.
Z: 2014 John Chambers <jc:trillian.mit.edu>
B: George Kauntze "Kauntze's Collection of the most favorite Dances, Reels, Waltzes, &c."
F: http://imslp.org/wiki/Kauntze%27s_Collection_of_Dances,_Reels,_Waltzes_etc._%28Various%29
N: This was published in London, some time in the late 1700s, but the actual year seems to be unknown.
N: The online photocopies are from a copy in the Biblioteca Nacional de Espa\~na.
N: Although the book isn't dated, there are several online dates of 1795.
K:
%%center Kauntze's
%%center Collection
%%center ----- of the most favorite -----
%%center Dances. Reels. Waltzes. &c.
%%center for the
%%center PIANO FORTE or HARP.  % %center
%%center BOOK I. -------------------------------------------------- Pr 2s.6
%%center Printed for T.Kauntze, Whitehall, opposite the Admiralty.
%%center -----------------------------------
%%begintext align
%% Transcription notes:
%% The tunes are are unnumbered; their count (01-24)
%% is used in the file name to preserve the publication order.
%% V:2 has the original staff breaks; V:1 has 4- and 8-bar staffs.
%% Dances are transcribed with the original line breaks, which isn't significant.
%% (I've seen claims that the original had 24 tunes, but I've only
%% found images for the first 19 of them. Tune 20 here is the alternate
%% version of tune 16, as marked up by some previous owner of the book.)
%%endtext

